<%#
  The ground passing under the runner, and the header's bottom rule in one.
  Scrolling it is what makes the figure read as travelling rather than running
  on the spot — four frames of legs cannot carry that on their own.

  The strip is far wider than the page so the clip never reaches its end, and
  the pattern repeats every two characters so the loop lands on itself.
%>
<div class="ascii-ground select-none font-mono text-sm leading-none text-rule <%= local_assigns[:classes] %>"
     aria-hidden="true">
  <pre class="ascii-ground__strip">~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-</pre>
</div>
